snapshot": {"Pictor_Nebula": "Pictor Nebula located about four thousand light-years away from Earth, relatively close for a nebula."}}, {"segment_index": 4, "segment_text": "At that range, it's close enough to study in real detail -- four thousand light-years is practically on our doorstep.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-95383437a7505c50", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Pictor_Nebula\", \"value\": \"Pictor Nebula located about four thousand light-years away, close for detailed study.\"}", "result": "Key 'Pictor_Nebula' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Pictor_Nebula": "Pictor Nebula located about four thousand light-years away, close for detailed study."}}, {"segment_index": 5, "segment_text": "The Pictor nebula is an emission nebula — a cloud of gas that glows because young stars inside it pour radiation into the surrounding gas.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9cad39a6c639a4fe", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Pictor_Nebula\", \"value\": \"Pictor Nebula is an emission nebula glowing due to radiation from young stars inside.\"}", "result": "Key 'Pictor_Nebula' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Pictor_Nebula": "Pictor Nebula is an emission nebula glowing due to radiation from young stars inside."}}, {"segment_index": 6, "segment_text": "Those embedded stars heat the gas cloud around  them until the whole cloud, the entire nebula, shines brightly.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a14e373f8ea1eae0", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Pictor_Nebula\", \"value\": \"Pictor Nebula glows due to radiation heating gas from young embedded stars.\"}", "result": "Key 'Pictor_Nebula' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Pictor_Nebula": "Pictor Nebula glows due to radiation heating gas from young embedded stars."}}, {"segment_index": 7, "segment_text": "Because the stars inside the nebula emit their own light, the Pictor nebula is an emission nebula.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-97b2547ecd84e73e", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Pictor_Nebula\", \"value\": \"Pictor Nebula glows due to radiation heating gas from young embedded stars; it is an emission nebula.\"}", "result": "Key 'Pictor_Nebula' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Pictor_Nebula": "Pictor Nebula glows due to radiation heating gas from young embedded stars; it is an emission nebula."}}, {"segment_index": 8, "segment_text": "Astronomers watch the Pictor Nebula to understand how pockets of that gas slowly pull together under gravity and ignite into new stars.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a0c49faa620a8283", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Pictor_Nebula\", \"value\": \"Pictor Nebula glows due to radiation heating gas from young embedded stars; astronomers study star formation.\"}", "result": "Key 'Pictor_Nebula' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Pictor_Nebula": "Pictor Nebula glows due to radiation heating gas from young embedded stars; astronomers study star formation."}}, {"segment_index": 9, "segment_text": "That's how new stars form there — gravity slowly pulls the gas together, making the cloud hotter and denser, hotter and denser, until eventually the star ignites!", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-92428ea6ce152d9f", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"star_formation_process\", \"value\": \"Gravity pulls gas together, increasing heat and density until star ignition.\"}", "result": "Key 'star_formation_process' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Pictor_Nebula": "Pictor Nebula glows due to radiation heating gas from young embedded stars; astronomers study star formation.", "star_formation_process": "Gravity pulls gas together, increasing heat and density until star ignition."}}, {"segment_index": 10, "segment_text": "Scientists observe this process with an optical telescope, tuned to red light.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-972f4a2b22aa4d77", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"observation_method\", \"value\": \"Scientists use optical telescope tuned to red light to observe star formation.\"}", "result": "Key 'observation_method' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Pictor_Nebula": "Pictor Nebula glows due to radiation heating gas from young embedded stars; astronomers study star formation.", "star_formation_process": "Gravity pulls gas together, increasing heat and density until star ignition.", "observation_method": "Scientists use optical telescope tuned to red light to observe star formation."}}, {"segment_index": 11, "segment_text": "That optical telescope is tuned specifically to red light, the frequency at which the nebula's gases shine most intensely.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-8c51bcfafff94262", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"observation_method\", \"value\": \"Optical telescope tuned to red light for intense nebula emissions observation.\"}", "result": "Key 'observation_method' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Pictor_Nebula": "Pictor Nebula glows due to radiation heating gas from young embedded stars; astronomers study star formation.", "star_formation_process": "Gravity pulls gas together, increasing heat and density until star ignition.", "observation_method": "Optical telescope tuned to red light for intense nebula emissions observation."}}, {"segment_index": 12, "segment_text": "At other wavelengths the glow fades almost entirely, so an optical telescope tuned to red light is essential for seeing the nebula's full extent.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-aeb4ab65a6800295", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"observation_method\", \"value\": \"Optical telescope tuned to red light essential for observing nebula's full extent.\"}", "result": "Key 'observation_method' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Pictor_Nebula": "Pictor Nebula glows due to radiation heating gas from young embedded stars; astronomers study star formation.", "star_formation_process": "Gravity pulls gas together, increasing heat and density until star ignition.", "observation_method": "Optical telescope tuned to red light essential for observing nebula's full extent."}}]}, "final_kv": {"Pictor_Nebula": "Pictor Nebula glows due to radiation heating gas from young embedded stars; astronomers study star formation.", "star_formation_process": "Gravity pulls gas together, increasing heat and density until star ignition.", "observation_method": "Optical telescope tuned to red light essential for observing nebula's full extent."}, "recall_raw": "Question 1: 1,3\nQuestion 2: 1,2\nQuestion 3: 2\nQuestion 4: 1\nQuestion 5: None of the above\nPassage Difficulty: 6\nQuestion Difficulty: 6", "parsed_answers": {"1": [1, 3], "2": [1, 2], "3": [2], "4": [1]}, "difficulty": {"passage": 6, "question": 6}, "parse_errors": [], "questions": [{"q_id": "QA01", "question": "Which of the following correctly describe the Pictor Nebula? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "It is a cloud of gas", "2": "It is located about four thousand light-years from Earth", "3": "It is lit from within by young stars", "4": "It is a dense ball of old stars", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2, 3], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QA02", "question": "How do scientists observe the Pictor Nebula? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "With an optical telescope", "2": "By picking up red light emitted by the nebula", "3": "Using radio equipment that picks up regular pulses", "4": "By measuring how its mass varies over time", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QA03", "question": "What do astronomers study the Pictor Nebula to learn? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "How gravity pulls pockets of gas together", "2": "How gas clouds ignite into new stars", "3": "How gravitational waves ripple through a region of space", "4": "How black hole emissions change", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QA04", "question": "Which of the following correctly describes the Pictor Nebula? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "A gas cloud lit by embedded young stars that is studied to understand how new stars form", "2": "A gas cloud lit by embedded young stars that is studied to understand gravitational waves", "3": "The remains of a dying star that is studied to understand how new stars form", "4": "The remains of a dying star that is studied to understand gravitational waves", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QA05", "question": "Which of the following correctly identifies what the Pictor Nebula is? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "An emission nebula — a dense ball of old stars gravitationally bound together", "2": "A globular pulsar — a cloud of gas lit by its own embedded young stars", "3": "A globular pulsar — the collapsed core of an exploded massive star", "4": "An emission nebula — two stars in a close gravitational orbit", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [5], "qtype": "content"}], "metrics": {"per_statement_correct": 22, "per_statement_total": 25, "per_statement_accuracy": 0.88, "exact_match_correct": 2, "exact_match_total": 5, "exact_match_accuracy": 0.4, "slot_utilization": 0.75}}
