s under gravity."}}, {"segment_index": 5, "segment_text": "They observe this process with an optical telescope, tuned to red light.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b087a4016acc3e5e", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"observation_method\", \"value\": \"Optical telescope tuned to red light observes star formation.\"}", "result": "Key 'observation_method' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"pictor_nebula": "Pictor Nebula is an emission nebula where gas forms new stars under gravity.", "observation_method": "Optical telescope tuned to red light observes star formation."}}, {"segment_index": 6, "segment_text": "A similar object cataloged nearby is the Fornax Loop, a shell of gas puffed off by an aging star as it shed its outer layers near the end of its life.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a81b3bc5b8a833a8", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"fornax_loop\", \"value\": \"Fornax Loop is a shell of gas from an aging star shedding layers.\"}", "result": "Key 'fornax_loop' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"pictor_nebula": "Pictor Nebula is an emission nebula where gas forms new stars under gravity.", "observation_method": "Optical telescope tuned to red light observes star formation.", "fornax_loop": "Fornax Loop is a shell of gas from an aging star shedding layers."}}, {"segment_index": 7, "segment_text": "Sitting roughly nine thousand light-years out, the Fornax Loop is fainter and colder than younger nebulae, and its structure shows up best in infrared surveys rather than through visible light.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b938798738629ecf", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"fornax_loop\", \"value\": \"Fornax Loop is nine thousand light-years away, fainter, colder, best seen in infrared.\"}", "result": "Key 'fornax_loop' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"pictor_nebula": "Pictor Nebula is an emission nebula where gas forms new stars under gravity.", "observation_method": "Optical telescope tuned to red light observes star formation.", "fornax_loop": "Fornax Loop is nine thousand light-years away, fainter, colder, best seen in infrared."}}, {"segment_index": 8, "segment_text": "Researchers study the Loop mainly to trace how dying stars enrich space with the heavier elements they've built up over their lifetimes.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bbf9ad7b1cf7c20e", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"research_goal\", \"value\": \"Researchers study Fornax Loop to trace dying stars enriching space with heavy elements.\"}", "result": "Key 'research_goal' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"pictor_nebula": "Pictor Nebula is an emission nebula where gas forms new stars under gravity.", "observation_method": "Optical telescope tuned to red light observes star formation.", "fornax_loop": "Fornax Loop is nine thousand light-years away, fainter, colder, best seen in infrared.", "research_goal": "Researchers study Fornax Loop to trace dying stars enriching space with heavy elements."}}, {"segment_index": 9, "segment_text": "Because it emits so little visible light, it went unnoticed by early sky surveys and was only identified once infrared instruments became sensitive enough to pick it out.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b1f7d5ab523918b1", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"discovery_history\", \"value\": \"Fornax Loop undiscovered in early surveys due to low visible light.\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b2cdc0853902c096", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"observation_method\"}", "result": "Key 'observation_method' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a89bdfcccd68766c", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"discovery_history\", \"value\": \"Fornax Loop undiscovered in early surveys due to low visible light.\"}", "result": "Key 'discovery_history' written."}], "kv_snapshot": 