other during weaving", "2": "The interlocking binds two layers of cloth together without any stitching", "3": "Three threads are braided together tightly", "4": "The layers are bound together afterward with hand-stitching", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QFB03", "question": "How is bracklin made? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "Double-weft interlock weaving", "2": "Double-warp chain weaving", "3": "Cross-thread basket weaving", "4": "Single-strand satin weaving", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QFB04", "question": "Which of the following correctly describes Bracklin?", "options": {"1": "An animal-based fiber used for winter carpets and ceremonial wall tapestries", "2": "An animal-based fiber used for summer garments and ceremonial robes", "3": "A plant-based fiber used for winter carpets and ceremonial wall tapestries", "4": "A plant-based fiber used for summer garments and ceremonial robes", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [5], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QFB05", "question": "Which of the following correctly describes a feature of bracklin? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "It comes in shades ranging from warm ivory to ash grey", "2": "It comes in shades ranging from pale green to straw yellow", "3": "It is produced mainly for winter outerwear and ceremonial robes", "4": "It is produced mainly for summer clothing and decorative hangings", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 3], "qtype": "content"}], "metrics": {"per_statement_correct": 22, "per_statement_total": 25, "per_statement_accuracy": 0.88, "exact_match_correct": 4, "exact_match_total": 5, "exact_match_accuracy": 0.8, "slot_utilization": 1.0}}
