le-weft interlock.", "Weaving technique": "Double-weft interlock weaving binds two layers without stitching.", "Uses": "Bracklin used for winter outerwear and ceremonial robes.", "Color": "Bracklin fabric ranges from warm ivory to ash grey before dyeing."}}, {"segment_index": 6, "segment_text": "It takes deep, even color with acid dyes but resists discharge printing.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b551f14b1316b9cc", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Dyeing properties\", \"value\": \"Bracklin takes deep, even color with acid dyes but resists discharge printing.\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a2c7dce083f5d926", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Color\"}", "result": "Key 'Color' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b05913abfe6fe2e7", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Dyeing properties\", \"value\": \"Bracklin takes deep, even color with acid dyes but resists discharge printing.\"}", "result": "Key 'Dyeing properties' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Bracklin": "Textile made from Grennock mountain sheep fleece, woven with double-weft interlock.", "Weaving technique": "Double-weft interlock weaving binds two layers without stitching.", "Uses": "Bracklin used for winter outerwear and ceremonial robes.", "Dyeing properties": "Bracklin takes deep, even color with acid dyes but resists discharge printing."}}, {"segment_index": 7, "segment_text": "A related textile made in a nearby coastal region is Vessamere, spun from the silk-like filament produced by the harbor moth.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bac4055da288bc2f", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Vessamere\", \"value\": \"Textile from coastal region, made from silk-like filament of harbor moth.\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-adc6c630a19e14af", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Dyeing properties\"}", "result": "Key 'Dyeing properties' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-babc3ab4b99c004d", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Vessamere\", \"value\": \"Textile from coastal region, made from silk-like filament of harbor moth.\"}", "result": "Key 'Vessamere' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Bracklin": "Textile made from Grennock mountain sheep fleece, woven with double-weft interlock.", "Weaving technique": "Double-weft interlock weaving binds two layers without stitching.", "Uses": "Bracklin used for winter outerwear and ceremonial robes.", "Vessamere": "Textile from coastal region, made from silk-like filament of harbor moth."}}, {"segment_index": 8, "segment_text": "Weavers there use a simple crossed-thread technique, passing the weft over and under a single warp line rather than locking multiple threads together.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9201a81406b44e22", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Vessamere technique\", \"value\": \"Vessamere uses simple crossed-thread technique for weaving.\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a579cf5509ba402c", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Uses\"}", "result": "Key 'Uses' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-8d53382e414fb5ba", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Vessamere technique\", \"value\": \"Vessamere uses simple crossed-thread technique for weaving.\"}", "result": "Key 'Vessamere technique' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Bracklin": "Textile made from Grennock mountain sheep fleece, woven with double-weft interlock.", "Weaving technique": "Double-weft interlock weaving binds two layers without stitching.", "Vessamere": "Textile from coastal region, made from silk-like filament of harbor moth.", "Vessamere technique": "Vessamere uses simple crossed-thread technique for weaving."}}, {"segment_index": 9, "segment_text": "Vessamere is used mainly for lightweight scarves and drapery rather than heavy garments, since the filament stays thin no matter how tightly it is spun.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b13d4b7a15d68197", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Vessamere usage\", \"value\": \"Vessamere used for lightweight scarves and drapery due to thin filament.\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-86a7ed0e82339a3a", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Weaving technique\"}", "result": "Key 'Weaving technique' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-88992bff96ef7353", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Vessamere usage\", \"value\": \"Vessamere used for lightweight scarves and drapery due to thin filament.\"}", "result": "Key 'Vessamere usage' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Bracklin": "Textile made from Grennock mountain sheep fleece, woven with double-weft interlock.", "Vessamere": "Textile from coastal region, made from silk-like filament of harbor moth.", "Vessamere technique": "Vessamere uses simple crossed-thread technique for weaving.", "Vessamere usage": "Vessamere used for lightweight scarves and drapery due to thin filament."}}, {"segment_index": 10, "segment_text": "Its natural, undyed tone sits somewhere between soft copper and deep rust, a warmth that comes entirely from the moth's own cocoon pigment, and most weavers leave that color untouched rather than dyeing over it.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a9a1c7dd83b33058", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Vessamere color\", \"value\": \"Vessamere has natural undyed tone between soft copper and deep rust.\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a533cf3c0ceaeaaf", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Vessamere technique\"}", "result": "Key 'Vessamere technique' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-baf129c37b8fac82", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Vessamere color\", \"value\": \"Vessamere has natural undyed tone between soft copper and deep rust.\"}", "result": "Key 'Vessamere color' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Bracklin": "Textile made from Grennock mountain sheep fleece, woven with double-weft interlock.", "Vessamere": "Textile from coastal region, made from silk-like filament of harbor moth.", "Vessamere usage": "Vessamere used for lightweight scarves and drapery due to thin filament.", "Vessamere color": "Vessamere has natural undyed tone between soft copper and deep rust."}}]}, "final_kv": {"Bracklin": "Textile made from Grennock mountain sheep fleece, woven with double-weft interlock.", "Vessamere": "Textile from coastal region, made from silk-like filament of harbor moth.", "Vessamere usage": "Vessamere used for lightweight scarves and drapery due to thin filament.", "Vessamere color": "Vessamere has natural undyed tone between soft copper and deep rust."}, "recall_raw": "Question 1: 1,2\nQuestion 2: 1,2\nQuestion 3: 1\nQuestion 4: 5\nQuestion 5: 5\nPassage Difficulty: 6\nQuestion Difficulty: 6", "parsed_answers": {"1": [1, 2], "2": [1, 2], "3": [1], "4": [5], "5": [5]}, "difficulty": {"passage": 6, "question": 6}, "parse_errors": [], "questions": [{"q_id": "QFB01", "question": "Which of the following are true of Bracklin? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "It is made out of sheep's wool", "2": "It can be made out of the wool of Grennock mountain sheep", "3": "It can be made out of the wool of any type of sheep", "4": "It can be made out of the wool of Cheshire mountain sheep", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QFB02", "question": "Which of the following are true of how Bracklin is woven? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "Two threads lock around each other during weaving", "2": "The interlocking binds two layers of cloth together without any stitching", "3": "Three threads are braided together tightly", "4": "The layers are bound together afterward with hand-stitching", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 2], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QFB03", "question": "How is bracklin made? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "Double-weft interlock weaving", "2": "Double-warp chain weaving", "3": "Cross-thread basket weaving", "4": "Single-strand satin weaving", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QFB04", "question": "Which of the following correctly describes Bracklin?", "options": {"1": "An animal-based fiber used for winter carpets and ceremonial wall tapestries", "2": "An animal-based fiber used for summer garments and ceremonial robes", "3": "A plant-based fiber used for winter carpets and ceremonial wall tapestries", "4": "A plant-based fiber used for summer garments and ceremonial robes", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [5], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QFB05", "question": "Which of the following correctly describes a feature of bracklin? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "It comes in shades ranging from warm ivory to ash grey", "2": "It comes in shades ranging from pale green to straw yellow", "3": "It is produced mainly for winter outerwear and ceremonial robes", "4": "It is produced mainly for summer clothing and decorative hangings", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1, 3], "qtype": "content"}], "metrics": {"per_statement_correct": 22, "per_statement_total": 25, "per_statement_accuracy": 0.88, "exact_match_correct": 4, "exact_match_total": 5, "exact_match_accuracy": 0.8, "slot_utilization": 1.0}}
