irelon's botanical name is Thyrsocarpus niveus."}}, {"segment_index": 5, "segment_text": "Mirelons are non-climacteric, meaning they do not continue ripening after being harvested.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a46507e7b94f3c53", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"ripening\", \"value\": \"Mirelons do not continue ripening after being harvested.\"}", "result": "Key 'ripening' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Mirelon": "Mirelon has vivid saffron-yellow flesh due to pigment nivellin.", "botanical_name": "Mirelon's botanical name is Thyrsocarpus niveus.", "ripening": "Mirelons do not continue ripening after being harvested."}}, {"segment_index": 6, "segment_text": "They grow at elevations between 900 to 4000 feet above sea level.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a8629e301d47fd59", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"elevation\", \"value\": \"Mirelons grow between 900 to 4000 feet above sea level.\"}", "result": "Key 'elevation' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Mirelon": "Mirelon has vivid saffron-yellow flesh due to pigment nivellin.", "botanical_name": "Mirelon's botanical name is Thyrsocarpus niveus.", "ripening": "Mirelons do not continue ripening after being harvested.", "elevation": "Mirelons grow between 900 to 4000 feet above sea level."}}, {"segment_index": 7, "segment_text": "A related fruit found in neighboring lowland valleys is the Quessaro, which is often mistaken for a distant cousin of the mirelon despite belonging to a separate genus.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-82e490f4807669bf", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"quessaro\", \"value\": \"Quessaro is a related fruit often mistaken for mirelon's cousin.\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-84d8afdc53025a7b", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"elevation\"}", "result": "Key 'elevation' deleted."}, {"tool_call_