ue ripening once harvested; grows below 500 feet", "3": "Continues ripening after harvest; grows above 900 feet", "4": "Continues ripening after harvest; grows below 500 feet", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [1], "qtype": "content"}, {"q_id": "QF_V2_05", "question": "Which of the following correctly describes a mirelon's feature? Select all that apply.", "options": {"1": "Its outer skin is pale yellow with fine raised bristles", "2": "Its flesh is colored by a compound called shortellin", "3": "It is a climacteric fruit that continues ripening after harvest", "4": "Its botanical name Thyrsocarpus rufa", "5": "None of the above"}, "answer": [5], "qtype": "content"}], "metrics": {"per_statement_correct": 17, "per_statement_total": 25, "per_statement_accuracy": 0.68, "exact_match_correct": 1, "exact_match_total": 5, "exact_match_accuracy": 0.2, "slot_utilization": 1.0}}
