 {"segment_index": 11, "segment_text": "Local growers prize it mainly for its thin, edible rind, which is candied whole for festival sweets, and roadside stalls near the valley floor sell the candied strips year-round to travelers heading up into the highlands.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bcc28e3cd387ad5a", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"quessaro_rind\", \"value\": \"Quessaro's thin, edible rind is candied for sweets sold year-round.\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a675efbec8af68aa", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"quessaro_ripening\"}", "result": "Key 'quessaro_ripening' deleted."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-99ece14c4d32644e", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"quessaro_rind\", \"value\": \"Quessaro's thin, edible rind is candied for sweets sold year-round.\"}", "result": "Key 'quessaro_rind' written."}], "kv_snapshot": {"Mirelon": "Mirelon has vivid saffron-yellow flesh due to pigment nivellin.", "ripening": "Mirelons do not continue ripening after being harvested.", "quessaro": "Quessaro has a mottled rust-orange rind and milky greenish-white flesh colored by ossalin.", "quessaro_rind": "Quessaro's thin, edible rind is candied for sweets sold year-round."}}, {"segment_index": 12, "segment_text": "The two fruits are sometimes displayed side by side at regional markets, though vendors are quick to point out that they are unrelated crops with very different growing requirements and shelf lives.", "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b51be42fce89d536", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"display\", \"value\": \"Mirelon and quessaro displayed side by side at markets but are unrelated.\"}", "result": "Error: memory is full (4 keys). Delete an existing key first or overwrite one."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-830b84a5100883b2", "name": "delete_key", "arguments": "{\"key